Thalira

Thank you for yesterday. A good meeting, if long.

Two things.

First, the Dean. I was not unkind, I hope, but I did not hear an answer and I=
 do not think the other members did either. Could you make sure he understand=
s that what I asked for is a short paper. Two pages. The figures by programme=
, what they intend to do, and how they will know whether it has worked. Not a=
 strategy. Not a vision. If Planning and Insight need to help him with the fi=
gures, so much the better; I would rather have their numbers than his.

Second, more generally. The pack for yesterday was 212 pages. I read it. I am=
 not confident everyone did. Could the Secretariat look at whether we can ask=
 authors for a one-page summary at the front of anything over ten pages, and =
whether the cover sheet word limit is being enforced. I know you will tell me=
 it is. I am asking whether it is working.

Papers deadline for May is the 12th, I think. Please hold the Dean to it.

With thanks

Aerion
